{"content": "What Needs to be Done Now: Eve of the Counterattack, Part 3 is the 16th episode of the 1st season and the 16th episode overall of the Attack on Titan anime, produced by Wit Studio and Production I.G.\n\nAfter the 104th cadets are investigated concerning the deaths of Sawney and Beane, they are presented with the choice of which regiment they will join. Commander Erwin, informing the cadets of the Scout Regiment's upcoming mission, urges for them to join their cause, and many cadets become official Scouts.\n\nEren later reunites with his friends and learns of Marco's death. One month later, the Scouts set out from Calaneth District on the 57th Exterior Scouting Mission.\n\nWith the two test subjects killed, the soldiers are being investigated for an unauthorized use of omni-directional mobility gear. A soldier cannot believe that one can get punished for killing Titans, but another one says that they were valuable test subjects for them after all. They point out that they were all tired and the cadets are being targeted. Armin says that in reality, this was a blow to mankind. Conny states that he kind of understands the motives of the culprit, stating that he never wants to see a Titan again despite initially wanting to join Scout Regiment. He then remembers the night of the battle when Eren decided that he was going to join the Scout Regiment as well.", "chunk_index": 0, "source_url": "https://attackontitan.fandom.com/wiki/What_Needs_to_be_Done_Now:_Eve_of_the_Counterattack,_Part_3", "source_title": "What Needs to be Done Now: Eve of the Counterattack, Part 3", "source_type": "episode", "episode_number": 16, "entity": null, "reveal_episode": 16, "embedding": [-0.01828017272055149, 0.07557935267686844, 0.04941723868250847, -0.049776531755924225, 0.06301230937242508, 0.02125128172338009, 0.015416772104799747, 0.019804878160357475, -0.034558918327093124, 0.030720852315425873, 0.024566082283854485, 0.011144297197461128, 0.06249263137578964, -0.0574710145592